  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "The temperature decreases by $1.2{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}$ each hour.\n\nSince the change is a decrease and occurs for $5$ hours, the total change can be written as repeated subtraction of $1.2:$\n\n$$\n{{-\\,1.2-1.2-1.2-1.2-1.2}_{⏟}}_{5\\text{ times}}\n$$\n\nRepeated subtraction can also be written using multiplication:\n\n$$\n5\\times (-1.2)\n$$\n\nEvaluating the product, we get\n\n$$\n5\\times (-1.2)=-6.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the total change in temperature after $5$ hours is $-6{\\,}^{∘}\\text{C}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
